 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to defining a victim of a\nsexual offense",
    "basePrintNo": "S7728",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7728-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §108, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7728\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to defining a victim of a\nsexual offense\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the definition of \"victims of a sexual offense\" to include\nvictims of revenge porn.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the definition of a \"victim of a sexual offense\" to\nmean a victim of any act constitution an offense as defined under arti-\ncle one hundred thirty, and/or sections 245.15, 255.25. 255.26, and\n255.27 of penal law, including threats or attempts to commit such\noffenses.\n\nSection 2 provides an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows for the expansion of the Address Confidentiality\nProgram to include victims of the revenge porn law, allowing them to\nutilize the ACP. The ACP is a program that assists individuals who have\nbeen victims of certain crimes and who have relocated as a result of the\ncrime. The ACP gives them an alternative address to use that would\nprotect the confidentiality of their location, and the inclusion of\nvictims under the revenge porn law allows for them to utilize the ACP\nduring the legal process.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.   \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately after it shall have become law.\n",
